{
    "title" : "Function Finale",
    "instructions": "Function Test",
    "instructionsHTML": "<div class=\"FormattedTextSection\">\n    <header class=\"hero\">\n        <h1>Functions Summary</h1>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">Bringing all three function concepts together</p>\n    </header>\n\n    <h2>Quick Review</h2>\n\n    <p>Before looking at combined examples, here is a concise summary of the three function concepts covered in this set.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"review-grid\">\n        <div class=\"review-card\">\n            <h3>What Is a Function</h3>\n            <ul>\n                <li>Defined with the <code>def</code> keyword</li>\n                <li>Has a name, parentheses, colon, and body</li>\n                <li>Definition does not run the code</li>\n                <li>Called by writing the name with <code>()</code></li>\n                <li>Always include a docstring</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"review-card\">\n            <h3>Parameters &amp; Arguments</h3>\n            <ul>\n                <li>Parameters are placeholders in the definition</li>\n                <li>Arguments are the values passed at the call</li>\n                <li>Multiple parameters separated by commas</li>\n                <li>Arguments are assigned in order</li>\n                <li>Parameters behave like variables inside the body</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n        <div class=\"review-card\">\n            <h3>Returning Data</h3>\n            <ul>\n                <li><code>return</code> sends a value back to the caller</li>\n                <li>The function ends immediately at <code>return</code></li>\n                <li>Without <code>return</code>, the function returns <code>None</code></li>\n                <li>Use <code>return</code> when the result is needed later</li>\n                <li>Return values can be stored, used in calculations, or passed on</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr>\n\n    <h2>Function Structure at a Glance</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n        <pre><code><span class=\"cm\"># Definition</span>\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">function_name</span>(<span class=\"var\">parameter1</span>, <span class=\"var\">parameter2</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"parameter1 description.\n    parameter2 description.\n    Describes what the function does and what it returns.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"cm\"># body — indented code that runs when called</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">some_value</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\"># Call</span>\n<span class=\"var\">result</span> = <span class=\"fn\">function_name</span>(<span class=\"var\">argument1</span>, <span class=\"var\">argument2</span>)</code></pre>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr>\n\n    <h2>Parameters and return Together</h2>\n\n    <p>The most common pattern in Python functions is to accept one or more parameters, perform a calculation or decision using them, and return the result.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n        <pre><code><span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">calculate_total</span>(<span class=\"var\">price</span>, <span class=\"var\">tax_rate</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"price is a positive number.\n    tax_rate is a percentage expressed as a whole number (e.g. 8 for 8%).\n    Returns the total price including tax.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"var\">tax</span> = <span class=\"var\">price</span> * (<span class=\"var\">tax_rate</span> / <span class=\"num\">100</span>)\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">price</span> + <span class=\"var\">tax</span>\n\n<span class=\"var\">shirt_total</span> = <span class=\"fn\">calculate_total</span>(<span class=\"num\">30</span>, <span class=\"num\">8</span>)\n<span class=\"var\">book_total</span> = <span class=\"fn\">calculate_total</span>(<span class=\"num\">15</span>, <span class=\"num\">5</span>)\n\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Shirt: $\"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">shirt_total</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Book: $\"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">book_total</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Combined: $\"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">shirt_total</span> + <span class=\"var\">book_total</span>))</code></pre>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr>\n\n    <h2>Functions with Conditions</h2>\n\n    <p>Functions regularly use <code>if/elif/else</code> inside their body to decide what to return. The parameter drives the condition, and the return value delivers the decision.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n        <pre><code><span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">admission_status</span>(<span class=\"var\">age</span>, <span class=\"var\">has_ticket</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"age is a positive int, has_ticket is a bool.\n    Returns a string describing the admission outcome.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">if</span> <span class=\"var\">age</span> &lt; <span class=\"num\">5</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"Free admission — no ticket needed.\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">elif</span> <span class=\"var\">has_ticket</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"Welcome in.\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">else</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"Ticket required.\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"fn\">admission_status</span>(<span class=\"num\">3</span>, <span class=\"bool\">False</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"fn\">admission_status</span>(<span class=\"num\">16</span>, <span class=\"bool\">True</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"fn\">admission_status</span>(<span class=\"num\">22</span>, <span class=\"bool\">False</span>))</code></pre>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr>\n\n    <h2>Functions with Loops</h2>\n\n    <p>A function body can contain a loop. The loop processes data locally, and the result is returned when the loop is complete.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n        <pre><code><span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">count_vowels</span>(<span class=\"var\">text</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"text is a string.\n    Returns the number of vowels in text.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"var\">vowels</span> = <span class=\"str\">\"aeiouAEIOU\"</span>\n    <span class=\"var\">count</span> = <span class=\"num\">0</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">for</span> <span class=\"var\">char</span> <span class=\"kw\">in</span> <span class=\"var\">text</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">if</span> <span class=\"var\">char</span> <span class=\"kw\">in</span> <span class=\"var\">vowels</span>:\n            <span class=\"var\">count</span> = <span class=\"var\">count</span> + <span class=\"num\">1</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">count</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\"># The return value can be stored and used further</span>\n<span class=\"var\">word1</span> = <span class=\"str\">\"programming\"</span>\n<span class=\"var\">word2</span> = <span class=\"str\">\"rhythm\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"var\">v1</span> = <span class=\"fn\">count_vowels</span>(<span class=\"var\">word1</span>)\n<span class=\"var\">v2</span> = <span class=\"fn\">count_vowels</span>(<span class=\"var\">word2</span>)\n\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"var\">word1</span> + <span class=\"str\">\": \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">v1</span>) + <span class=\"str\">\" vowel(s)\"</span>)\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"var\">word2</span> + <span class=\"str\">\": \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">v2</span>) + <span class=\"str\">\" vowel(s)\"</span>)\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Total: \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">v1</span> + <span class=\"var\">v2</span>))</code></pre>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr>\n\n    <h2>Calling One Function from Another</h2>\n\n    <p>Well-designed programs are built from small functions that each do one thing. Larger functions call smaller ones, combining their results to produce more complex behaviour.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n        <pre><code><span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">letter_grade</span>(<span class=\"var\">score</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"score is a number from 0 to 100.\n    Returns the letter grade as a string.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">if</span> <span class=\"var\">score</span> &gt;= <span class=\"num\">90</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"A\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">elif</span> <span class=\"var\">score</span> &gt;= <span class=\"num\">80</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"B\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">elif</span> <span class=\"var\">score</span> &gt;= <span class=\"num\">70</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"C\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">else</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"F\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">is_passing</span>(<span class=\"var\">score</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"score is a number from 0 to 100.\n    Returns True if the grade is C or better, False otherwise.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"fn\">letter_grade</span>(<span class=\"var\">score</span>) != <span class=\"str\">\"F\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">student_summary</span>(<span class=\"var\">name</span>, <span class=\"var\">score</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"name is a string, score is a number from 0 to 100.\n    Prints a full summary for one student.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"var\">grade</span> = <span class=\"fn\">letter_grade</span>(<span class=\"var\">score</span>)\n    <span class=\"var\">passing</span> = <span class=\"fn\">is_passing</span>(<span class=\"var\">score</span>)\n\n    <span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Student: \"</span> + <span class=\"var\">name</span>)\n    <span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Score: \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">score</span>))\n    <span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Grade: \"</span> + <span class=\"var\">grade</span>)\n    <span class=\"kw\">if</span> <span class=\"var\">passing</span>:\n        <span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Status: Passing\"</span>)\n    <span class=\"kw\">else</span>:\n        <span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Status: Not passing\"</span>)\n    <span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"---\"</span>)\n\n<span class=\"fn\">student_summary</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Alex\"</span>, <span class=\"num\">91</span>)\n<span class=\"fn\">student_summary</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Sam\"</span>, <span class=\"num\">74</span>)\n<span class=\"fn\">student_summary</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Jordan\"</span>, <span class=\"num\">58</span>)</code></pre>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr>\n\n    <h2>A Complete Example — Quiz Scorer</h2>\n\n    <p>This program uses three functions together. Each handles one responsibility: collecting input, computing a score, and reporting results. Notice how each function is short, focused, and clearly named.</p>\n\n    <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n        <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n        <pre><code><span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">collect_scores</span>(<span class=\"var\">num_questions</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"num_questions is a positive int.\n    Asks the user to enter a score for each question.\n    Returns the total points as an int.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"var\">total</span> = <span class=\"num\">0</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">for</span> <span class=\"var\">q</span> <span class=\"kw\">in</span> <span class=\"fn\">range</span>(<span class=\"num\">1</span>, <span class=\"var\">num_questions</span> + <span class=\"num\">1</span>):\n        <span class=\"var\">points</span> = <span class=\"fn\">int</span>(<span class=\"fn\">input</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Points for question \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">q</span>) + <span class=\"str\">\": \"</span>))\n        <span class=\"var\">total</span> = <span class=\"var\">total</span> + <span class=\"var\">points</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">total</span>\n\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">calculate_percentage</span>(<span class=\"var\">total</span>, <span class=\"var\">possible</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"total is the points earned, possible is the maximum points.\n    Returns the percentage as a float.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> (<span class=\"var\">total</span> / <span class=\"var\">possible</span>) * <span class=\"num\">100</span>\n\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">result_label</span>(<span class=\"var\">percentage</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"percentage is a float from 0 to 100.\n    Returns a result label as a string.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">if</span> <span class=\"var\">percentage</span> &gt;= <span class=\"num\">90</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"Distinction\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">elif</span> <span class=\"var\">percentage</span> &gt;= <span class=\"num\">70</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"Merit\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">elif</span> <span class=\"var\">percentage</span> &gt;= <span class=\"num\">50</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"Pass\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">else</span>:\n        <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"str\">\"Did not pass\"</span>\n\n<span class=\"cm\"># Main program — calls all three functions</span>\n<span class=\"var\">num_q</span> = <span class=\"fn\">int</span>(<span class=\"fn\">input</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"How many questions? \"</span>))\n<span class=\"var\">points_each</span> = <span class=\"fn\">int</span>(<span class=\"fn\">input</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Points per question: \"</span>))\n\n<span class=\"var\">earned</span> = <span class=\"fn\">collect_scores</span>(<span class=\"var\">num_q</span>)\n<span class=\"var\">possible</span> = <span class=\"var\">num_q</span> * <span class=\"var\">points_each</span>\n<span class=\"var\">pct</span> = <span class=\"fn\">calculate_percentage</span>(<span class=\"var\">earned</span>, <span class=\"var\">possible</span>)\n<span class=\"var\">label</span> = <span class=\"fn\">result_label</span>(<span class=\"var\">pct</span>)\n\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Points earned: \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">earned</span>) + <span class=\"str\">\" / \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">possible</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Percentage: \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"fn\">round</span>(<span class=\"var\">pct</span>, <span class=\"num\">1</span>)) + <span class=\"str\">\"%\"</span>)\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Result: \"</span> + <span class=\"var\">label</span>)</code></pre>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"callout callout-note\">\n        <div class=\"callout-title\"><span>i</span> Note — One Responsibility Per Function</div>\n        <div class=\"callout-body\">\n            Each function in the example above does exactly one thing: collecting input, computing a percentage, or labelling a result. This makes each function easy to read, test, and change independently. If the grading scale changes, you only update <code>result_label</code>.\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <hr>\n\n    <h2>Practice</h2>\n\n    <div class=\"callout callout-try\">\n        <div class=\"callout-title\"><span>&#9654;</span> Try This — Unit Converter</div>\n        <div class=\"callout-body\">\n            <p>These two functions convert between miles and kilometres. Run the program, then add a third function called <code>conversion_summary</code> that takes a distance in miles and prints both the original value and the converted value.</p>\n            <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n                <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n                <pre><code><span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">miles_to_km</span>(<span class=\"var\">miles</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"miles is a positive number.\n    Returns the equivalent distance in kilometres.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">miles</span> * <span class=\"num\">1.60934</span>\n\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">km_to_miles</span>(<span class=\"var\">km</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"km is a positive number.\n    Returns the equivalent distance in miles.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">km</span> / <span class=\"num\">1.60934</span>\n\n<span class=\"var\">distance_miles</span> = <span class=\"fn\">float</span>(<span class=\"fn\">input</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Enter a distance in miles: \"</span>))\n<span class=\"var\">in_km</span> = <span class=\"fn\">miles_to_km</span>(<span class=\"var\">distance_miles</span>)\n\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">distance_miles</span>) + <span class=\"str\">\" miles = \"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"fn\">round</span>(<span class=\"var\">in_km</span>, <span class=\"num\">2</span>)) + <span class=\"str\">\" km\"</span>)</code></pre>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"callout callout-try\">\n        <div class=\"callout-title\"><span>&#9654;</span> Try This — Shopping Cart</div>\n        <div class=\"callout-body\">\n            <p>This program uses two functions to calculate the cost of a shopping order. Run it, then add a third function called <code>apply_discount</code> that takes a total and a discount percentage and returns the reduced price.</p>\n            <div class=\"code-wrap\">\n                <div class=\"code-toolbar\"><span class=\"code-lang\">Python</span><button class=\"copy-btn\" onclick=\"copyCode(this)\">Copy</button></div>\n                <pre><code><span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">item_total</span>(<span class=\"var\">price</span>, <span class=\"var\">quantity</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"price is the cost of one item, quantity is how many.\n    Returns the total cost for this item.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">price</span> * <span class=\"var\">quantity</span>\n\n<span class=\"kw\">def</span> <span class=\"fn\">add_tax</span>(<span class=\"var\">subtotal</span>, <span class=\"var\">rate</span>):\n    <span class=\"str\">\"\"\"subtotal is a positive number, rate is a percentage.\n    Returns the subtotal with tax added.\"\"\"</span>\n    <span class=\"kw\">return</span> <span class=\"var\">subtotal</span> + (<span class=\"var\">subtotal</span> * (<span class=\"var\">rate</span> / <span class=\"num\">100</span>))\n\n<span class=\"var\">pens</span> = <span class=\"fn\">item_total</span>(<span class=\"num\">1.50</span>, <span class=\"num\">4</span>)\n<span class=\"var\">notebook</span> = <span class=\"fn\">item_total</span>(<span class=\"num\">4.99</span>, <span class=\"num\">2</span>)\n<span class=\"var\">subtotal</span> = <span class=\"var\">pens</span> + <span class=\"var\">notebook</span>\n<span class=\"var\">total</span> = <span class=\"fn\">add_tax</span>(<span class=\"var\">subtotal</span>, <span class=\"num\">8</span>)\n\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Pens: $\"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">pens</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Notebooks: $\"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">notebook</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Subtotal: $\"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"var\">subtotal</span>))\n<span class=\"fn\">print</span>(<span class=\"str\">\"Total with tax: $\"</span> + <span class=\"fn\">str</span>(<span class=\"fn\">round</span>(<span class=\"var\">total</span>, <span class=\"num\">2</span>)))</code></pre>\n            </div>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"callout callout-try\">\n        <div class=\"callout-title\"><span>&#9654;</span> Try This — Write Your Own</div>\n        <div class=\"callout-body\">\n            <p>Write a small program that uses at least three functions together. Choose a topic you find interesting — a sports scoring system, a recipe cost calculator, a fitness tracker, or anything else. Your program must include:</p>\n            <ul>\n                <li>At least one function with two or more parameters</li>\n                <li>At least one function that uses <code>return</code></li>\n                <li>At least one function that uses an <code>if/elif/else</code> block</li>\n                <li>A docstring on every function</li>\n                <li>At least three function calls that use the returned values</li>\n            </ul>\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <div class=\"callout callout-tip\">\n        <div class=\"callout-title\"><span>i</span> Where to Go From Here</div>\n        <div class=\"callout-body\">\n            You now have a solid foundation: variables, conditions, loops, and functions. These four concepts are present in virtually every Python program ever written. From here, common next topics include lists and dictionaries for storing collections of data, file handling for reading and writing files, and modules for using code written by others.\n        </div>\n    </div>\n\n    <footer>Based on UAI Module 1 — Python Coding Basics &nbsp;|&nbsp; Ana Bell, MIT &nbsp;|&nbsp; Copyright MIT 2025</footer>\n\n</div>",
